# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the C++ tests (configure --enable-sanitizers).
#
# serialize_function/directory_restored reads a deliberately truncated
# archive. Boost.Serialization (1.90, iserializer.hpp) gives up ownership of
# an object loaded through a pointer before its data is read, so when the
# archive ends partway through it, nothing frees it. A load error path in
# Boost, accepted (implementation_plan.md, ST finding B). Needs
# ASAN_OPTIONS=fast_unwind_on_malloc=0 for the full stack, which make check
# sets.
leak:directory_restored
